<title>USA: Pentech settles legal judgment.</title>
<headline>Pentech settles legal judgment.</headline>
<dateline>EDISON, N.J. 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pentech International Inc said on Friday it settled the previously announced adverse legal judgment related to a patent.  </p>
<p>The company said it has been involved in a patent infringement case with Paradise over a pack of six colored markers, with another marker which could erase the ink of the other pens.</p>
<p>Pentech said it had filed a lawsuit against Paradise and Paradise filed a counterclaim.</p>
<p>Pentech said it paid $500,000 and delivered its promissory note for $3 million, payable $100,000 per quarter. Pentech also said it obtained rights to the patent that was the subject of the lawsuit, pursuant to a five year license with a 10 percent royalty.</p>
</text>
